    Bug 2045132 - Set the delivery format and keep saved drafts in their authored format. r=mkmelin


    The send/save API created messages with the wrong delivery format in
    X-Mozilla-Draft-Info, and HTML drafts were saved as plain text. This patch
    addresses both issues:

    - compFields.deliveryFormat is the persistent format intent, written to
      X-Mozilla-Draft-Info and used to restore the editor mode when a draft
      or template is reopened. It is now always set to a specific value derived
      from the requested format, instead of being left at Unset (4):
      - auto/unspecified -> Auto (0)
      - plaintext -> PlainText (1)
      - html -> HTML (2)
      - both -> Both (3)

    - forcePlainText/useMultipartAlternative shape the MIME produced when
      sending. They are applied for send modes (where we keep the auto downgrade
      code*) and for pure plain text. An HTML save now leaves them at their
      defaults, so a draft or template keeps its HTML body and reopens in the
      HTML composer instead of plain text.

    * Why the auto downgrade code is kept, despite the suggestion in bug 1545930
      comment 45 to drop it: The compose window decides whether to downgrade HTML
      to plain text from a convertibility check on the editor:

      determineSendFormat() -> bodyConvertible(), which is just nodeTreeConvertible()
      on the editor's root

      The Mail Merge Experiment Add-on therefore used the downgrade feature of the
      editor. It is not the send backend doing the downgrade. Since the send/save
      API does not use an editor, it has to do the same downgrade check manually.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D304949

